    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **273 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the sequential membership number for newly created owners. Each new owner is assigned `membershipNumber = (current number of owners) + 1`, returned as an integer field `membershipNumber` in the owner response.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` (integer, int32) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` (and MapStruct mapping, which matches by name) picks it up automatically.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring the existing `registrationDate` pattern.\n\n3. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 In `saveOwner`, for new owners only (alongside the existing registration-date assignment), set `owner.setMembershipNumber(ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1)`.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 Added a `membership_number` column to the `owners` table. HSQLDB is what the test suite uses; the others were updated for consistency.\n\nThe new `Cp09Tests` acceptance test (asserting two consecutive creations differ by exactly one) passes, as does the entire existing suite.",
